            <ArticleTitle>Effect of polymyxin B-containing regimens on renal function for the treatment of carbapenem-resistant Enterobacteriacea mediastinitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1413-8670(17)30709-2</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bjid.2017.10.006</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A retrospective cohort study, were evaluated: polymyxin B plus aminoglycosides or polymyxin B plus other antibiotics. Any degree of acute kidney injury occurred in 26 (86.6%) patients. The median time to acute kidney injury was 6.0 (95% CI 3-14) days in the polymyxin-aminoglycoside containing regimen group, against 27.0 (95% CI 6-42) days in the polymyxin with other antimicrobial combinations group (p=0.03). Polymyxin B with aminoglycosides group progressed faster to any degree of renal dysfunction.</AbstractText>
